    "result_text": "Everything is wired correctly. The implementation is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the age-band feature so the request may include `birthDate` (ISO) and the owner response returns a derived `ageBand`.\n\n**Design \u2014 logic placed where it belongs, reusing the existing derived-field pattern:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional, `format: date`) to the input `OwnerFields` schema, and `ageBand` (read-only `string` enum `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs, API interface, and validation are code-generated from this spec.\n\n2. **`model/AgeBand.java`** (new) \u2014 a small single-responsibility enum that owns the classification rule: `AgeBand.asOf(birthDate, asOf)` computes completed years via `Period.between` and maps to `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+).\n\n3. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the stored `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with accessors, plus a `@Transient getAgeBand()` derived getter alongside the existing derived getters (`getContactPreference`, `getLocality`, etc.). It delegates to `AgeBand.asOf(...)` against `registrationDate`, returning `null` when `birthDate` is absent.\n\n4. **Schema SQL** \u2014 added `birth_date DATE` to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres).\n\nMapStruct picked everything up automatically: `birthDate` maps both directions, and the model `AgeBand` enum maps to the generated `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum` by name (null-safe). No controller/service changes were needed \u2014 `registrationDate` is already resolved before the response is mapped, so the derived band is correct at creation.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the new `coreDerivesAgeBand` acceptance test asserting `ageBand == \"ADULT\"` for a 1990 birthdate).",
